# A context-format half ("*** x" then "--- y") opens the operand ahead of a
# real CRLF section with two hunks; the "*** x" line alone ends in bare LF, so
# the whole-operand predicate never fired here. The half is refused at the
# tail, after every later line was compacted in place, and the diagnostic
# names it without its CR: the saved view survived the compaction of
# everything behind it.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 1
